3039       *----------------- Data on Physical Fitness -----------------*
3040       | These measurements were made on men involved in a physical |
3041       | fitness course at N.C. State University. |
3042       | Only selected variables of |
3043       | Oxygen (oxygen intake, ml per kg body weight per minute), |
3044       | Runtime (time to run 1.5 miles in minutes), and |
3045       | RunPulse (heart rate while running) are used. |
3046       | Certain values were changed to missing for the analysis. |
3047       *------------------------------------------------------------*;
3048       data Fitness1;
3049       input Oxygen RunTime RunPulse @@;
3050       datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.FITNESS1 has 31 observations and 3 variables.

3067       ;
3068       proc mi data=Fitness1 seed=3237851 noprint out=outmi;
3069       var Oxygen RunTime RunPulse;
3070       run;

WARNING: The default number of imputations has been changed from 5 to 25.
NOTE: The EM algorithm (MLE) converges in 12 iterations.
NOTE: The EM algorithm (posterior mode) converges in 7 iterations.
NOTE: The data set WORK.OUTMI has 775 observations and 4 variables.

3071       proc reg data=outmi outest=outreg covout noprint;
3072       model Oxygen= RunTime RunPulse;
3073       by _Imputation_;
3074       run;

NOTE: Interactivity disabled with BY processing.
NOTE: The data set WORK.OUTREG has 100 observations and 10 variables.

3075       proc print data=outreg(obs=8);
3076       var _Imputation_ _Type_ _Name_
3077       Intercept RunTime RunPulse;
3078       title 'Parameter Estimates from Imputed Data Sets';
3079       run;

NOTE: There were 8 observations read from the data set WORK.OUTREG.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE PRINT printed page 268.

3080       proc mianalyze data=outreg;
3081       modeleffects Intercept RunTime RunPulse;
3082       run;

